Subject: Backend Changes Required – Advanced Tooltip Configuration for Charts

Hi Team,

As part of the enhanced tooltip implementation for our charts, we need two additional parameters to be provided in the API response under views.chart:

{
  "advanceTooltip": true,
  "tooltipConfig": {
    "mode": "table",
    "categoryLabel": "FS Type",
    "columns": [
      {
        "key": "mc",
        "label": "MC ($MM)",
        "seriesPrefix": "MC "
      },
      {
        "key": "hist",
        "label": "Hist ($MM)",
        "seriesPrefix": "Hist "
      }
    ],
    "removeSeriesPrefixes": ["MC ", "Hist "],
    "footerSeriesContains": "cvar trend",
    "sortDescending": true,
    "valueDecimals": 1
  }
}

advanceTooltip will be a boolean flag to determine whether the UI should use the new advanced/table tooltip functionality. When it is true, the UI will read and apply tooltipConfig. When it is false or not provided, the existing/default tooltip behaviour can be used.

Details of the tooltipConfig properties:

* mode – Defines the tooltip display format. Currently "table" indicates that the tooltip should be rendered in tabular format.
* categoryLabel – Heading/label for the category column in the tooltip, for example "FS Type".
* columns – Defines the dynamic value columns that should be displayed in the tooltip.
    * key – Unique identifier for the tooltip column, e.g. "mc" or "hist".
    * label – Display heading for that column, e.g. "MC ($MM)".
    * seriesPrefix – Prefix used to identify which chart series belongs to this column, e.g. "MC " or "Hist ".
* removeSeriesPrefixes – List of prefixes that should be removed from the series name while displaying the category/FS Type. For example, "MC EQDL" can be displayed as "EQDL".
* footerSeriesContains – Text used to identify the series that should be displayed separately as the tooltip footer. For example, a series containing "cvar trend" will be treated as footer information.
* sortDescending – Boolean flag indicating whether tooltip rows should be sorted in descending order based on their values.
* valueDecimals – Number of decimal places to use while displaying numeric values. For example, 1 will display a value as 123.4.

This configuration will allow the frontend tooltip implementation to remain generic and API-driven rather than having chart-specific values hardcoded in the UI.

